# RES-53: Genuine process kill restores the reader from disk state.
#
# The page must come back from the PdfRecord row through
# DocumentLoader.findPageNumber, so phase two must not be handed the page
# number. It reads it from the app's own storage, which survives because
# clearPackageData is off after phase one.
describe Genuine process kill restores the reader from disk state

# Opens normal.pdf, scrolls to page index 15, waits for the record column to
# agree, then presses Home so the app is in the background.
phase com.gitlab.mudlej.MjPdfReader.suite.resilience.ProcessKillRestoreTest#phaseOneReadToTargetPage

kill-app
# Avoid both a resolver race and phase-two instrumentation force-stopping the
# reader by issuing the explicit PDF launch after the phase reports started.
launch-view-after-start file:///sdcard/Download/normal.pdf

# Asserts page index 15 restored from disk, and that SearchSessionCache has nothing,
# which is what proves the process really was replaced.
phase com.gitlab.mudlej.MjPdfReader.suite.resilience.ProcessKillRestoreTest#phaseTwoAssertRestoredFromDisk
